WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.640
DataIQ, iMBrace’s records boards, holds the fictional company’s brand rules.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.680
Connect the brief. A submitted status starts the campaign workflow.

3
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:22.120
The saved board automation connects the submitted brief to its workflow.

4
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.840
Give the writer its brand guide. The prepared skill reads the active brand rules.

5
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.800
The prepared skill reads the selected brand-rules board.

6
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:39.680
Check the draft before approval. Brand checks guide revision before the copy reaches review.

7
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:46.440
The brand check guides revision before the copy reaches approval.

8
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.460
Connect the writer and its skill. The assistant uses the saved brand-guide skill.

9
00:00:52.460 --> 00:01:04.240
The fictional campaign brief shows the completed writing and review workflow.

10
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:11.440
The saved brief carries its recorded approval.

11
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:18.640
The approval identifies the held version and the automated demo role.

12
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:25.920
The revised draft passes the configured brand checks.

13
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:33.160
The brief lists the requested claims left out of the copy.

14
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.680
Approved channel copy stays on the brief for the publishing team.

15
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.720
Inspect the recorded decision. The decision stays with the checked copy.

16
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:56.560
The decision records the automated test acting as marketing approver.

17
00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.080
The decision resumes the waiting workflow for this copy version.

18
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:10.200
Follow the completed workflow. The draft, brand check and decision share one workflow.

19
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.460
The original workflow completes with its recorded decision.
